[CHANGE] benchmark_1/parts/dag_engine_lite/lib/dag_engine_lite.py: Implemented the DAG engine interface module: added @data_type/@operation/@singleton_type framework decorators and contract docstrings matching low/dag_engine_lite.pyi. Converted the five exception data types (DAGError, CycleError, NodeNotFoundError, DuplicateNodeError, NodeExecutionError) from frozen to plain @dataclass semantics to satisfy pyright's frozen-exception constraint while preserving __str__ messages; kept frozen dataclasses for value types NodeDefinition/NodeResult/DAGRunReport and the NodeState/FailurePolicy enums.
[CHANGE] benchmark_1/parts/dag_engine_lite/lib/dag_engine_lite_impl.py: Realized DAG, WaveScheduler, and DAGRunner from low/dag_engine_lite_impl.pyi. DAG: adjacency-backed add_node/add_edge/remove_node with DuplicateNodeError/NodeNotFoundError preconditions, DFS cycle detection, priority-desc/asc Kahn topological_sort, and longest-weight critical-path DP. WaveScheduler: state sync, ready-wave resolution, mark transitions, and FAIL_FAST (cancel non-terminal) / SKIP_DOWNSTREAM / CONTINUE_ON_ERROR policies. DAGRunner: validate-then-wave execution with retries, failure-policy propagation, and DAGRunReport construction. Collaborators resolved via get_singleton; broad-exception retry handler marked cleanroom:allow-broad-exception.
[CHANGE] benchmark_1/parts/dag_engine_lite/pretense/dag_engine_lite_pretense.py: Implemented faithful DagEngineLite interface state machine (DAG/WaveScheduler/DAGRunner). Replaced Domain.required scaffolding with concrete domains (not_in/in_set/type/optional/sampled_from) and replaced _unimplemented_transition pivots with real model-derived return values. Added module-level model helpers (cycle detection, Kahn topo sort, critical-path DP, wave simulation) and a DagEngineLiteState modeling nodes/edges/scheduler states. Postconditions asserted with single-arg asserts; contracted errors (DuplicateNode/NodeNotFoundError, cycle) gated via require/require_arg.
[CHANGE] benchmark_1/parts/dag_engine_lite/pretense/dag_engine_lite_impl_pretense.py: Resolved DagEngineLite impl target: replaced self.fail placeholder with granular real-implementation scenarios (TestDagEngineLiteImplReal) driving all operations via self.checked adapters — graph register/query, edges, removal, topo order, critical path, wave chain execution, and all three failure policies (FAIL_FAST, SKIP_DOWNSTREAM, CONTINUE_ON_ERROR), plus runner success/failure/retry/empty-graph coverage. Added FailurePolicy/NodeState/typing imports; removed dag_engine_lite qualified refs.
[BLAME] benchmark_1/parts/dag_engine_lite/pretense/dag_engine_lite_pretense.py: In dag_engine_lite_pretense.py the sequential wave-simulation helper _simulate_run (lines 188-277) fails to satisfy the WaveScheduler.mark_succeeded postcondition defined in low/dag_engine_lite.pyi (operation 413-414), which requires that completing a node MUST evaluate its downstream dependents and promote newly unblocked nodes to READY; when a node action succeeds the simulation stores NodeState.SUCCEEDED for that node but never promotes any PENDING dependent to READY, so the subsequent _ready_nodes() evaluation over the local state yields no further ready wave and dependents are never executed. For a graph whose node b depends on node a under FailurePolicy.FAIL_FAST where both actions succeed, the post-wave default-fill loop at lines 257-262 skips b because its local state remains PENDING (a non-terminal state) and is therefore never inserted into results, so the report assembly at line 264 raises KeyError b instead of constructing a DAGRunReport. This violates DAGRunner.run's postcondition in low/dag_engine_lite.pyi (operation 481-505) that the run MUST return a consolidated report capturing every node's state, meaning the interface state machine models the wave-promotion contract incorrectly rather than faithfully mirroring the scheduler's promote-unblocked-dependents obligation.
[CHANGE] benchmark_1/parts/dag_engine_lite/pretense/dag_engine_lite_pretense.py: Resolved feedback: added wave-promotion to _simulate_run so that when a node action succeeds it evaluates downstream dependents and promotes newly-unblocked PENDING dependents to READY (mirroring WaveScheduler.mark_succeeded postcondition low/dag_engine_lite.pyi:413-414). Previously dependents stayed PENDING after their predecessor succeeded, so no subsequent ready wave formed and the post-wave default-fill loop skipped them, causing a KeyError on report assembly and violating DAGRunner.run's return-all-states postcondition (481-505). Now dependents are promoted, executed, and captured in the DAGRunReport. Note: bin/check_files currently fails at module-import collection with an environmental pydantic ImportError (identical failure on the sibling impl target; pydantic lives in site-packages outside the workspace); the logic fix is verified by code review and git diff.
