[BLAME] benchmark_1/parts/dag_engine_lite/lib/dag_engine_lite_impl.py: Per the low-level specification, line 77 in lib/dag_engine_lite_impl.py is a checked precondition raise (it raises dag_engine_lite.NodeNotFoundError when node_id is absent from the graph), which the spec explicitly designates as an untestable caller violation: conforming callers are guaranteed node_id is registered, so no conforming test can exercise this span. The methodology therefore requires it to be annotated '# pragma: no cover (assumption: precondition enforced by caller)', exactly as the equivalent precondition guards in the same file already are at line 72 (get_node) and line 83 (get_dependents). The author's # CHANGE did not address this: it added self._sync_states() at the start of mark_failed to synchronize the scheduler state before the FAIL_FAST cancellation loop and re-synced registration to regenerate CODE_HASH, which is why FAIL_FAST cancellation and the previously uncovered public postconditions are now covered, but it left the get_dependencies precondition raise at line 77 unannotated, so statement coverage still stalls at 99.6% below the 100% threshold. Annotate line 77 with the precondition assumption pragma to reach full coverage.
